  "plain": "The CIA, the US foreign intelligence agency founded in the 1940s, was the idea of the people at Brown Brothers Harriman, a private Wall Street bank, according to a guest named Dan Sheehan. Sheehan says it without naming a source: the agency \"was the brainchild of the people at Brown Brothers Harriman.\" If true, it would mean American intelligence was shaped from the start by private banking interests."
